%description:

Tcp.limitedTransmitEnabled:on -- the first duplicate ACK sends a new segment.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Limited Transmit algorithm (RFC 3042) enabled/disabled".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false; LegacyTcp). The code: a new segment at
each of the first dupthresh - 1 duplicate ACKs (TcpAlgorithmBase::receivedDuplicateAck(),
Rfc6675Recovery). This test separates "on" from "off".

Host under test: host1, which sends 30000 bytes with an initial window of three segments; the
tap drops the first one, so host2 answers the two others with duplicate ACKs. Observation:
level 1, the first segment that host1 sends after the first duplicate ACK is new data: the
fourth segment.

%# parameter: Tcp.limitedTransmitEnabled
%# class: on
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.limitedTransmitEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpLimitedTransmitEnabledOn")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength == tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first duplicate ACK at host1")
             .within(1.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 3 * 1448")
             .describe("the next segment of host1, the fourth one")
             .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpLimitedTransmitEnabledOn compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.limitedTransmitEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 30000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpLimitedTransmitEnabledOn: PASS
